  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Unsettled weather will persist throughout this \nweek with daily chances of showers and thunderstorms.\n\nWatching a cluster of storms entering northwest WV, surging\nsouthward at 30 to 40 mph. SPC mesoanalysis and a couple high\nres models have this activity reaching Bath/Greenbrier between\n3pm-4pm, other models have little or no convection but are not\npicking up on current situation.\n\nThinking is bumping pops up across our northwest CWA this\nafternoon, then decrease them quickly to the southeast as all\nmodels break this convection up and main support pushes across\nnorthern VA. However, one model does keep the MCS sinking\nsouthward into the rest of the CWA though 03z, and may blend in\nthat with the current forecast keeping at least chance pops\nelsewhere.\n\nUpper pattern keeps a trough from the mid-Atlantic north into\nthe Canada, with ridge set up from Texas to the southeast coast.\n\nSeveral embedded vorts, some convective induced will track from\nthe Ohio Valley/Midwest into our area for the next couple of\ndays. Strong to severe storms possible Tuesday with good shear,\nbut limiting factor could be morning convection and upper clouds\nthat may limit sunshine. Still any sunshine will lead to SBCAPEs\nin the 1000-2000 J/kg range, and seems enough to overall keep\npops higher over WV per model trends. Temps/dewpoints were\nlowered from NBM Tuesday with downsloping and cloud cover.\n\nAlthough convective activity diminishes a little in intensity \nand coverage towards the end of this week, sufficient \ninstability and orographical lift will ensure that storm chances\nlinger throughout the upcoming weekend.",
